.TH zbasic 1 "Zanna" "zbasic" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zbasic \- compile or run Zanna BASIC source files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zbasic
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIFILE.bas\fR [\fB--\fR \fIprogram-args...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBzbasic\fR is the single-file Zanna BASIC driver. It runs BASIC source
through the BASIC frontend and either executes the program, emits textual IL,
or produces native output when \fB-o\fR names a non-\fB.il\fR file.
.PP
For project, directory, REPL, and packaging workflows, use \fBzanna\fR(1).
.PP
Invoking \fBzbasic\fR without a source file prints command help and exits. It
does not enter a REPL; use \fBzanna repl basic\fR for an interactive session.
.SH MODES
.TP
Run (default)
\fBzbasic\fR \fIFILE.bas\fR
.TP
Emit IL to stdout
\fBzbasic\fR \fIFILE.bas\fR \fB--emit-il\fR
.TP
Emit IL or native output to file
\fBzbasic\fR \fIFILE.bas\fR \fB-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-o\fR, \fB--output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Write IL when \fIFILE\fR ends in \fB.il\fR; otherwise compile native output.
.TP
\fB--emit-il\fR
Emit IL instead of running the program.
.TP
\fB--trace\fR[=\fIil\fR|\fIsrc\fR]
Enable tracing.
.TP
\fB--bounds-checks\fR
Enable array bounds checks (default for source).
.TP
\fB--no-bounds-checks\fR
Disable generated source bounds checks.
.TP
\fB--stdin-from\fR \fIFILE\fR
Redirect stdin from file.
.TP
\fB--max-steps\fR \fIN\fR
Limit instruction steps.
.TP
\fB--dump-trap\fR
Show detailed trap diagnostics.
.TP
\fB--diagnostic-format\fR \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR
Select diagnostic output format.
.TP
\fB--paranoid-verify\fR
Run all frontend verifier checkpoints.
.TP
\fB--pass-stats\fR
Print optimizer pass statistics.
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Show command help and exit.
.TP
\fB--version\fR
Show version information and exit.
.SH NOTES
FUNCTIONs must return on all paths; SUBs cannot be used as expressions; array
parameters are ByRef. The shared Zia warning-control flags are accepted for CLI
compatibility but do not change BASIC diagnostics.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a source file
.nf
zbasic hello.bas
.fi
.TP
Emit IL to stdout
.nf
zbasic hello.bas --emit-il
.fi
.TP
Save IL to a file
.nf
zbasic hello.bas -o hello.il
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBzanna\fR(1), \fBzia\fR(1), \fBilrun\fR(1)
